{"Tests don't catch this bug because they mock datasource.runQuery so super.query() and its applyTemplateVariables call never execute, and the mock applyTemplateVariables does an idempotent string replace that hides the duplication": 0.8099270462989807, "The new applyTemplateVariables call in runSplitQuery (line 298) causes ad-hoc filters to be duplicated on every split query, because DataSourceWithBackend.query() also calls applyTemplateVariables downstream, and addAdHocFilters unconditionally appends filter clauses without deduplication": 0.889936089515686, "For shard-split queries, applyTemplateVariables is called three times (runShardSplitQuery + runSplitQuery + DataSourceWithBackend.query), tripling the ad-hoc filters": 0.7900058627128601, "The fix should remove the applyTemplateVariables call from runSplitQuery and runShardSplitQuery, relying solely on the existing call in DataSourceWithBackend.query()": 0.7139366269111633}